{#
	The plain-text half of a signup confirmation (XIV-64).

	Written by hand rather than derived from the HTML one, for the reason the
	invitation's text part gives: a text part made by stripping tags out of a
	table layout is a text part nobody would want to read.

	The URL is on its own line and nothing else is, because that is what makes a
	mail client turn it into something clickable — and this message has exactly
	one job.
#}
